    "conclusions": {
      "feasibility": "Each deflated critical zero imposes 2 real linear constraints Re(E_b) = 0 and Im(E_b) = 0. Together with 1^T b = 0, deflating k zeros requires 2k + 1 independent constraints. In the 4-grade family (dim 4), at most 1 zero can be deflated (leaving dim 1). In 6 grades, at most 2 zeros can be deflated (leaving dim 1). In 8 grades, at most 3 zeros can be deflated (leaving dim 1). As the number of deflated zeros increases, the constraint condition number deteriorates rapidly (cond ~1556 for 3 zeros in 8 grades), causing oscillatory coefficients in higher grades and preventing unconstrained localization without inflation of the remaining spectral tail."
